ter Writing Program Wyndham Alumnae House The Latest toggle submenu Bryn Mawr Today Events Submit Your Event Online/Virtual Event Guide Announcements Submit Your Announcement Academic and Other College Calendars Policies, Guidelines, and Handbooks toggle submenu College Policies and Guidelines Handbooks and Catalogs Sexual Misconduct Open Location menu Visit Guide Visit Information Interactive Campus Map Maps and Directions Open Tools menu Tools & Resources Moodle BiONiC Library Tripod Webmail Academic and Other College Calendars Open Resources menu Resources For Prospective Undergraduates Current Students Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty/Staff and Department Directories Faculty & Staff Directory Search Student Directory (BiONiC) Search Search Breadcrumb Inside Bryn Mawr Home Academic Information Office of the Provost Open Faculty Positions Section In This Section Assistant Professor of Political Science Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of Psychology Assistant Professor of Political Science The Department of Political Science at Bryn Mawr College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in American (U.S.) Politics to begin August 1, 2027. We are open to candidates working in a wide range of areas, but we are particularly interested in those whose research examines extra-governmental organizations - such as political parties, interest groups, and media - or scholars with an interest in public opinion, political behavior, and elections. The successful candidate will maintain an active research agenda and teach American politics at the introductory and advanced levels, including 300-level seminars and courses in quantitative and mixed methods. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in research and undergraduate teaching and have completed all Ph.D. requirements by the start date. To apply for this position, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching philosophy, writing sample, and a sample syllabus to the Political Science Department Search Committee via Interfolio at: https://apply.interfolio.com/189862 . In addition, arrange for three letters of recommendation to be submitted via Interfolio to the Political Science Department Search Committee. Applications received by October 1, 2026, will receive full consideration. Apply via Interfolio Political Science Take the Next Step How to Apply Request Information Schedule a Tour Ways to Give Back to top 101 North Merion Ave. Bryn Mawr, PA 19010-2899 (610) 526-5000 Contact Us Facebook Instagram Youtube Linkedin Tiktok Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Directory Libraries & Collections Bookshop Athletics Events Calendar Newsroom Plan a Visit Campus Map Make a Gift Careers at Bryn Mawr © 2026 Bryn Mawr College. All rights reserved. Footer Protest and Demonstration Resources Report a Website Issue Title IX Web Accessibility Land Acknowledgement"
