lege Writing Center Writing Program Wyndham Alumnae House The Latest toggle submenu Bryn Mawr Today Events Submit Your Event Online/Virtual Event Guide Announcements Submit Your Announcement Academic and Other College Calendars Policies, Guidelines, and Handbooks toggle submenu College Policies and Guidelines Handbooks and Catalogs Sexual Misconduct Open Location menu Visit Guide Visit Information Interactive Campus Map Maps and Directions Open Tools menu Tools & Resources Moodle BiONiC Library Tripod Webmail Academic and Other College Calendars Open Resources menu Resources For Prospective Undergraduates Current Students Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty/Staff and Department Directories Faculty & Staff Directory Search Student Directory (BiONiC) Search Search Breadcrumb Inside Bryn Mawr Home Academic Information Office of the Provost Open Faculty Positions Section In This Section Assistant Professor of Political Science Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of Psychology Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of Psychology The Department of Psychology at Bryn Mawr College invites applications for a full-time, tenure- track Assistant or Associate Professor position to begin August 1, 2027, in Behavioral Neuroscience. The successful candidate will be expected to have a robust research agenda that will engage undergraduate students. The area of research specialty is open, but we have a preference for candidates whose research engages questions about linkages between the brain and behavior in animal models. We are interested in broadly trained candidates who will enhance departmental offerings in biological areas and strengthen the department’s contributions to the Bi-College (Bryn Mawr College and Haverford College) major in Neuroscience. The successful candidate will supervise student research and teach across the curriculum, including an introductory course in neuroscience, an intermediate-level survey course in behavioral neuroscience, an advanced course in the candidate’s areas of expertise, and a research methods laboratory course in behavioral neuroscience. A Ph.D. in Psychology, Neuroscience, or a closely related field is required by the start date, and post-doctoral research experience is desirable. To apply for this position, candidates must submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and a research statement to the Psychology Department Search Committee via Interfolio at: https://apply.interfolio.com/189819 . Applications received by September 13, 2026, will receive full consideration. In addition, candidates should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be submitted via Interfolio to the Psychology Department Search Committee. Apply via Interfolio Psychology Take the Next Step How to Apply Request Information Schedule a Tour Ways to Give Back to top 101 North Merion Ave. Bryn Mawr, PA 19010-2899 (610) 526-5000 Contact Us Facebook Instagram Youtube Linkedin Tiktok Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Directory Libraries & Collections Bookshop Athletics Events Calendar Newsroom Plan a Visit Campus Map Make a Gift Careers at Bryn Mawr © 2026 Bryn Mawr College. All rights reserved. Footer Protest and Demonstration Resources Report a Website Issue Title IX Web Accessibility Land Acknowledgement"
