      "title": "Advanced Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of the Growth and Structure of Cities",
      "description": "Advanced Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of the Growth and Structure of Cities Skip to main content Grad Programs and More Bryn Mawr Home Graduate & Postbac Graduate School of Arts and Sciences Graduate School of Social Work and Social Research Postbaccalaureate Premedical Program Inside Bryn Mawr Menu Grad Programs and More Bryn Mawr Home Graduate & Postbac Graduate School of Arts and Sciences Graduate School of Social Work and Social Research Postbaccalaureate Premedical Program Inside Bryn Mawr Main Academic Information toggle submenu Departments and Programs Special Academic Programs Research Graduate and Postbac Office of the Provost Registrar Catalog Graduation Requirements Offices and Services toggle submenu Academic Support Access Services Admissions Alumnae/i Relations and Development Arts at Bryn Mawr Athletics and Physical Education Board of Trustees Bookshop at Bryn Mawr College Bulletin Campus Safety Career & Civic Engagement Center CARLA — Coalition for Anti-Racist Literacy Child Study Institute Civil Rights and Title IX Communications & Marketing Conferences and Events One-on-One Consultations Ask Athena How-To Digital Competencies Dining Services Educational & Scholarly Technology Environmental Health and Safety Facilities Financial Aid Finance and Administration First-Year Experience General Counsel Global Engagement Graduate Admissions Health and Wellness Center Health Professions Advising Human Resources Information Technology Institutional Research, Planning, and Assessment Investment Office Junior Experience Library & Information Technology Services Mailroom Noyce Teacher Scholarship Program OneCard Peer Tutors Performing Arts Series Phebe Anna Thorne School Posse at Bryn Mawr President's Office Quantitative Center Reading Series Residential Life Senior Experience Science Support Services Sophomore Experience Staff Association Student Accounts Student Engagement Student Success Sustainability Office Impact Center Transportation Undergraduate College Writing Center Writing Program Wyndham Alumnae House The Latest toggle submenu Bryn Mawr Today Events Submit Your Event Online/Virtual Event Guide Announcements Submit Your Announcement Academic and Other College Calendars Policies, Guidelines, and Handbooks toggle submenu College Policies and Guidelines Handbooks and Catalogs Report Sexual Misconduct Resources Sexual Misconduct Policy Open Location menu Visit Guide Visit Information Interactive Campus Map Maps and Directions Open Tools menu Tools & Resources Moodle BiONiC Library Tripod Webmail Academic and Other College Calendars Open Resources menu Resources For Prospective Undergraduates Current Students Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty/Staff and Department Directories Faculty & Staff Directory Search Student Directory (BiONiC) Search Search Breadcrumb Inside Bryn Mawr Home Academic Information Office of the Provost Open Faculty Positions Section In This Section Advanced Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of the Growth and Structure of Cities Assistant Professor of Political Science Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of Psychology Advanced Assistant Professor or Associate Professor of the Growth and Structure of Cities The Growth and Structure of Cities Department at Bryn Mawr College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track advanced Assistant Professor or Associate Professor to begin August 1, 2027. The candidate should have a preferred specialization in environmental issues with attention to the social dynamics of cities and processes of urban place-making. We are most interested in scholars who can synthesize urban and environmental analyses into an understanding of the human and spatial dynamics of the built landscape. Geographic specialization is open. We seek a scholar who is able to develop a robust research agenda that complements the department’s interdisciplinary curriculum that spans the social sciences to histories and design of built landscapes at multiple scales; the candidate should also be able to teach with and alongside faculty in this interdisciplinary context. Demonstrated experience with and/or commitment to community development and public scholarship, especially related to the Philadelphia region is a plus. In addition to teaching experience, the candidate must have demonstrated leadership skills and curriculum development experience. A completed Ph.D. in a social science field is required by the start date. To apply for this position, candidates must submit (1) a cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) research statement, (4) teaching statement, (5) sample course proposal or syllabus, and (6) writing sample (such as a published article or dissertation) to the Growth and Structure of Cities Department Search Committee via Interfolio at: https://apply.interfolio.com/196087 . In addition, candidates should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be submitted via Interfolio to the Growth and Structure of Cities Department Search Committee. Applications received by January 4, 2027, will receive full consideration. Apply via Interfolio Growth and Structure of Cities Take the Next Step How to Apply Request Information Schedule a Tour Ways to Give Back to top 101 North Merion Ave. Bryn Mawr, PA 19010-2899 (610) 526-5000 Contact Us Facebook Instagram Youtube Linkedin Tiktok Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Directory Libraries & Collections Bookshop Athletics Events Calendar Newsroom Plan a Visit Campus Map Make a Gift Careers at Bryn Mawr © 2026 Bryn Mawr College. All rights reserved. Footer Protest and Demonstration Resources Report a Website Issue Web Accessibility Land Acknowledgement"
